        "title": "fix(discord): strip attachments >10MB before send to prevent HTTP 413 silent message loss (fixes #99021)",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes #99021.\n\n## Changes Made\n\n1. send.shared.ts: Pre-flight size check strips attachments > 10 MB\n2. send.outbound.ts: receipt kind reflects mediaStripped flag\n3. send.receipt.ts: Added mediaStripped field to result type\n4. 3 regression tests\n\n## Evidence (commit: 7b9203db45)\n\n### Real Discord API proof (live bot)\nBEFORE: 11MB file -> HTTP 413 -> message lost\nAFTER: Size check -> text delivered, receipt kind: text (not media)\n\n### Unit tests (47/47 passed)\n- strips oversized media >10MB\n- respects configured mediaMaxMb >10MB\n- sends text-only fallback\n\n## AI Assistance\n- AI-assisted: Yes\n",
